Backport of the nlohmann/json fixes for the stack overflow on deeply nested values
(https://github.com/nlohmann/json/issues/5387) onto v3.12.0. Copying, dump() and
comparing a value nested deep enough would crash with SIGSEGV.

Applied by scripts/sync_vendor.py after downloading json.hpp.

TODO: remove this patch once nlohmann/json releases a version newer than 3.12.0

Contents, from the upstream develop branch:
- copy:    56b3ee566 (#5389), 67435c9c7 (#5721)
- dump():  d6e521af6 (the "Bound the descent of dump()" commit of #5285), ported to the
           v3.12.0 serializer, which does not have the write buffer of #5285
- compare: 02dd3e67f (#5390)

